---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Colophon"
  description="How this site is built — the stack, typography, hosting, and principles behind alaabadr.net."
>
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-b from-peach-cream/60 to-warm-white py-20 md:py-28 border-b border-warm-blush">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <p class="font-caveat text-2xl text-burnt-sienna mb-3">How this site is made</p>
      <h1 class="font-fraunces text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl text-deep-brown mb-6 leading-tight">
        Colophon
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-warm-umber leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        A short page about the tools and choices behind this site &mdash; for the curious and the craft-minded.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-warm-white py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 md:gap-16">
      <!-- Stack -->
      <div>
        <div class="w-10 h-1 rounded-full mb-3 bg-forest-teal"></div>
        <h2 class="font-fraunces text-3xl text-deep-brown mb-5">Stack</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2.5 text-warm-umber">
          <li><strong class="text-deep-brown">Framework:</strong> Astro 5 with Content Collections</li>
          <li><strong class="text-deep-brown">Styling:</strong> Tailwind CSS 3</li>
          <li><strong class="text-deep-brown">Hosting:</strong> Cloudflare Pages &mdash; free tier, unlimited bandwidth</li>
          <li><strong class="text-deep-brown">Images:</strong> <code class="bg-peach-cream/60 rounded px-1 py-0.5 text-sm">astro:assets</code> + Sharp, self-hosted for reliability</li>
          <li><strong class="text-deep-brown">Feeds:</strong> <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a> via <code class="bg-peach-cream/60 rounded px-1 py-0.5 text-sm">@astrojs/rss</code></li>
          <li><strong class="text-deep-brown">Sitemap:</strong> <code class="bg-peach-cream/60 rounded px-1 py-0.5 text-sm">@astrojs/sitemap</code></li>
          <li><strong class="text-deep-brown">Analytics:</strong> Cloudflare Web Analytics, privacy-respecting, no cookies</li>
          <li><strong class="text-deep-brown">Source:</strong> Markdown + MDX in a git repo</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Typography -->
      <div>
        <div class="w-10 h-1 rounded-full mb-3 bg-burnt-sienna"></div>
        <h2 class="font-fraunces text-3xl text-deep-brown mb-5">Typography</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2.5 text-warm-umber">
          <li><strong class="text-deep-brown">Display &amp; body:</strong> <em class="font-fraunces">Fraunces</em> (variable). One typeface, two jobs &mdash; the OPSZ axis lets the same font handle headlines and long-form reading.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-deep-brown">UI / sans:</strong> <em class="font-lato">Lato</em></li>
          <li><strong class="text-deep-brown">Accent:</strong> <em class="font-caveat text-xl">Caveat</em> &mdash; used sparingly, for margin notes</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4 text-warm-umber text-sm">All three self-hosted via <code class="bg-peach-cream/60 rounded px-1 py-0.5">@fontsource</code>. No external font requests, no Google Fonts handshake.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Palette (full width) -->
      <div class="md:col-span-2">
        <div class="w-10 h-1 rounded-full mb-3 bg-marigold"></div>
        <h2 class="font-fraunces text-3xl text-deep-brown mb-5">Palette</h2>
        <p class="text-warm-umber mb-6 max-w-2xl">Warm earth tones &mdash; peach cream, warm umber, burnt sienna, forest teal, dusty rose, marigold. Built for the 2026 move away from gradient-dark-mode sameness, toward sites that feel like places.</p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-6 gap-4">
          {[
            { name: 'warm-white', hex: '#FFFBF5', cls: 'bg-warm-white border border-warm-blush' },
            { name: 'peach-cream', hex: '#FFF3E8', cls: 'bg-peach-cream' },
            { name: 'warm-umber', hex: '#8A7362', cls: 'bg-warm-umber' },
            { name: 'burnt-sienna', hex: '#C96B3C', cls: 'bg-burnt-sienna' },
            { name: 'forest-teal', hex: '#4A7C72', cls: 'bg-forest-teal' },
            { name: 'marigold', hex: '#E8A944', cls: 'bg-marigold' },
          ].map((c) => (
            <div>
              <div class={`aspect-square rounded-xl ${c.cls} shadow-sm`}></div>
              <p class="mt-2 text-xs font-lato font-bold text-deep-brown">{c.name}</p>
              <p class="text-xs font-lato text-warm-umber/70">{c.hex}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Principles -->
      <div class="md:col-span-2">
        <div class="w-10 h-1 rounded-full mb-3 bg-dusty-rose"></div>
        <h2 class="font-fraunces text-3xl text-deep-brown mb-5">Principles</h2>
        <ul class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-3 text-warm-umber">
          <li>Ship honestly &mdash; no fake content, no placeholder links masquerading as real ones.</li>
          <li>Zero JavaScript by default. Islands only where interaction earns them.</li>
          <li>Own the audience &mdash; RSS + newsletter + email, never a single-platform bet.</li>
          <li>IndieWeb-friendly: rel=me, h-card microformats, planned webmentions.</li>
          <li>AI-crawler opt-out by default in <a href="/robots.txt">robots.txt</a>.</li>
          <li>Respect the reader's time, bandwidth, and attention.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Credits -->
      <div class="md:col-span-2 pt-8 border-t border-warm-blush/60">
        <p class="text-sm text-warm-umber/80">
          Built by <a href="/">Alaa Badr</a>. Influenced by Craig Mod, Paul Stamatiou, Maggie Appleton, Robin Rendle, Lynn Fisher, and the whole IndieWeb crowd. Placeholder imagery from Unsplash, self-hosted for reliability; will be replaced with original photography as real content ships.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
